      "content": "1.Guidelines as Topic – standards. 2.Review. 3.Meta-Analysis. 4.Peer Review. 5.Evidence-Based \nMedicine. 6.World Health Organization. I.World Health Organization. \nISBN 978 92 4 154896 0\t\t\t\n(NLM classification: WA 39)\nAcknowledgements\nThis handbook was prepared by Susan L. Norris. Laragh Gollogly and Charles Penn provided advice and support throughout the \ndevelopment process. Contributions in the areas of equity, human rights, gender and social determinants were made in this edition \nof the handbook (including Chapter 5) by the WHO Gender, Equity and Human Rights mainstreaming team (acknowled",
