    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-070",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "What is a guideline planning proposal?",
      "pageStart": 51,
      "pageEnd": 51,
      "target": "../sections/sec-070-41-what-is-a-guideline-planning-proposal.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "A guideline planning proposal is a document that outlines the rationale and \nscope of a proposed guideline and the methods and resources involved in \ndeveloping it. The proposal includes many of the components of a protocol for \na systematic review and guideline, plus additional information on the groups \ncontributing to guideline development and the administrative steps required \nfor WHO guidelines. The responsible technical officer must submit a planning proposal to the GRC for each guideline to be developed and the GRC’s \napproval is required for guideline development to proceed to completi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines a guideline planning proposal as a document outlining the rationale, scope, methods and resources of a proposed guideline, including protocol-like components plus information on contributing groups and administrative steps. States that the technical officer must submit one to the review committee for each guideline and that its approval is required for development to proceed to completion.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-071",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "What is the purpose of the planning proposal?",
      "pageStart": 51,
      "pageEnd": 51,
      "target": "../sections/sec-071-42-what-is-the-purpose-of-the-planning-proposal.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "To embark on any project or produce any document, including guidelines, \nits developers need an explicit, thoughtful and comprehensive plan or roadmap. The planning proposal serves several important purposes.\nFirst, a planning proposal helps to ensure that a high-quality and credible guideline is produced. The GRC and the Secretariat can provide constructive feedback, which helps to ensure that the final guideline will meet \nWHO standards. In addition, many steps in guideline development must \nbe performed correctly early in the process, since they cannot generally be \nremedied later, and a pl",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains why a planning proposal is needed, giving reasons including securing early feedback on a credible guideline, setting its relationship to existing WHO guidelines, and avoiding overlap. Adds that it smooths the process by matching resources to scope, promotes accountability and protects integrity by fixing methods in advance and limiting bias.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-072",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Preparing the planning proposal",
      "pageStart": 51,
      "pageEnd": 52,
      "target": "../sections/sec-072-4-preparing-the-planning-proposal.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "39\nThird, a carefully constructed planning proposal makes it more likely that \nthe guideline development process will be smooth and efficient. Resources \nwill closely match the proposed scope; relevant expertise will be identified \nand engaged early and throughout the development process; and potential difficulties, both procedural and technical, can be anticipated and planned for.\nFourth, the planning proposal promotes accountability. When the scope, \nmethods and timeline of the guideline are laid out and approved by the steering group a priori, each member of the steering group and the direc",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues the reasons for a planning proposal, saying it makes development smoother and more efficient, promotes accountability through an agreed scope, methods and timeline, and above all promotes the integrity of the process. States that deciding methods in advance reduces arbitrariness and bias and that mid-stream method changes driven by findings or dominant members must be avoided.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-073",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Who develops the planning proposal?",
      "pageStart": 52,
      "pageEnd": 52,
      "target": "../sections/sec-073-43-who-develops-the-planning-proposal.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The responsible technical officer in the technical unit leading the guideline",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States that the responsible technical officer in the leading technical unit develops the planning proposal; the sentence continues onto the next page.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-074",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Preparing the planning proposal",
      "pageStart": 52,
      "pageEnd": 53,
      "target": "../sections/sec-074-45-preparing-the-planning-proposal.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "close collaboration with other members of the steering group. Broad input \nmust be obtained, however, to ensure a useful product. The GDG, or at least \na subset of that group including the chair, should provide input into the \nguideline’s scope and key questions in PICO format. The systematic review \nteam and the guideline methodologist should also provide input into the key \nquestions before they are finalized. It may also be useful to have members of \nthe external review group provide input.\nIf resources allow, the GDG may meet in person before the planning \nproposal is finalized to define t",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Says the technical officer prepares the proposal in close collaboration with the steering group but must obtain broad input. Names the development group chair, the systematic review team, the methodologist and possibly the external review group as contributors to the key questions, and notes the group may meet in person, virtually or by email to define scope and methods.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-075",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "When should the planning proposal be developed and finalized?",
      "pageStart": 53,
      "pageEnd": 55,
      "target": "../sections/sec-075-44-when-should-the-planning-proposal-be-develope.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "and finalized?\nThe planning proposal is the first major product of the guideline development process, and its preparation starts as soon as the technical unit decides \nto develop a guideline. The responsible technical officer should strive to \ndevelop and submit the proposal to the GRC for review as quickly as possible, but with sufficient consideration and preparation of the many elements \nin the proposal. The most difficult and time-consuming part of the planning \nproposal is formulating the key questions (in PICO format). These questions \nneed to be well developed in the planning proposal,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
