    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-082",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Background",
      "pageStart": 57,
      "pageEnd": 59,
      "target": "../sections/sec-082-52-background.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The WHO Constitution (2) states that:\n“Health is a state of complete physical, mental and social well-being \nand not merely the absence of disease or infirmity.”\nand that\n“The enjoyment of the highest attainable standard of health is \none of the fundamental rights of every human being without \ndistinction of race, religion, political belief, economic or social \ncondition.” \nGuideline developers need to consider how their guidelines will contribute to the realization of the right to health, as we shall henceforth refer to the \nconcept embodied in the second of these statements. In so doing, the",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives the background to the chapter, quoting the WHO Constitution on health and the right to the highest attainable standard of health and saying developers should consider how guidelines advance that right. Defines equity as unfair and avoidable inequalities and discusses measuring them, and begins describing human rights dimensions of the right to health, including its freedoms and entitlements.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
