      "target": "../sections/sec-113-72-formulating-key-questions-in-pico-format.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "PICO is an acronym for population, intervention (or exposure), comparator and outcome − four elements that should be considered in any question \ngoverning a systematic search of the evidence. Sometimes T is added for the \ntiming of the measurement of outcomes or for the duration of the intervention \nor exposure, and S for the setting where the recommendations will be implemented (PICOTS). For simplicity we use PICO in this handbook, wrapping",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines PICO as population, intervention or exposure, comparator and outcome, and mentions the PICOTS variant adding timing and setting. The text breaks off mid-sentence at the end of the section.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
