    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-114",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Intervention or exposure",
      "pageStart": 91,
      "pageEnd": 93,
      "target": "../sections/sec-114-722-intervention-or-exposure.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "the P (population) or the I. The PICO format also provides a useful structure \nfor delineating inclusion and exclusion criteria for the body of evidence (see \nChapter 8) and for formulating recommendations (see Chapter 10).\n7.2.1 Population\nWhat group or population is targeted by the intervention or exposure \nunder consideration?\n■■\nHow can the members of the target population be most accurately \ndescribed? What are the relevant demographic characteristics? Consider age, sex and other social, geographic and environmental characteristics that are of relevance to the guideline topic.\n■■\nWhat is",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Extraction put text under a heading that covers only part of it: it finishes the PICO introduction by noting that PICO also structures inclusion criteria and recommendations. It then lists guiding questions for the population element (demographics, setting, subpopulations) and for the intervention or exposure element (what treatment, policy or determinant is evaluated and at what levels).",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
