      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "References",
      "pageStart": 104,
      "pageEnd": 105,
      "target": "../sections/sec-131-79-references.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "1.\t\nGuyatt GH, Oxman AD, Vist GE, Kunz R, Falck-Ytter Y, Alonso-Coello P, et al.; GRADE \nWorking Group. GRADE: an emerging consensus on rating quality of evidence and \nstrength of recommendations. BMJ. 2008;336(7650):924–6. doi: http://dx.doi.org/10.1136/\nbmj.39489.470347.AD PMID: 18436948\n2.\t\nNational Institute for Health and Clinical Excellence. The guidelines manual – Chapter 4. \nLondon: National Institute for Health and Clinical Excellence; 2012 (http://www.nice.org.\nuk/article/pmg6, accessed 11 November 2014).\n3.\t\nGuyatt GH, Oxman AD, Santesso N, Helfand M, Vist G, Kunz R, et al. GRADE gu",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A reference list of five sources for the question-formulation chapter, including GRADE, NICE guideline manual and US Preventive Services Task Force papers. The extraction also appends the opening paragraphs of the next chapter, which state that WHO recommendations must rest on the best available evidence and on a systematic review guided by key questions.",
        "state": "draft",
