      "narrative": null,
      "content": "It is not always necessary to commission a new systematic review (see \nFig. 8.1). If one or more relevant, current and high-quality systematic reviews \nexist, these should be used. Updates, if needed, are usually less expensive and \ntime-consuming than new reviews.\nWHO handbook for guideline development\n96",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States that a new systematic review is not always needed, since relevant, current and high-quality existing reviews should be used and updates are usually cheaper and faster than new reviews. The extraction also includes page-header text.",
