        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains how the steering group assesses existing systematic reviews for relevance (by comparing each PICO component with the guideline's key question), quality and timeliness before deciding whether a new review is needed. It names the AMSTAR, R-AMSTAR and Oxman and Guyatt checklists, warns against using them as scoring tools, and says there is no fixed rule for dismissing a review as out of date. The extraction includes the text of Figure 8.1, a yes-or-no decision flowchart.",
