      "target": "../sections/sec-141-step-3-select-studies-and-abstract-data.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "As the first stage in selecting relevant studies, records retrieved from the \nbibliographic databases and from other sources are recorded and assessed \nfor eligibility by examining their titles and abstracts only. This assessment is \nperformed in accordance with the inclusion and exclusion criteria developed \na priori. The full text of articles found to be potentially relevant on the basis \nof their titles and abstracts is retrieved and examined in light of the same \ninclusion criteria in the second stage of study selection. Data from eligible \nstudies are then extracted into pre-defined templ",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes step 3: screening records by title and abstract and then by full text against criteria set in advance, followed by extraction of data into predefined templates, with at least two people working independently. It also requires documenting databases, strategies, counts and exclusion reasons, and showing the flow of studies in a PRISMA diagram.",
