      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Including qualitative research",
      "pageStart": 115,
      "pageEnd": 116,
      "target": "../sections/sec-145-84-including-qualitative-research.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Qualitative data can address certain types of key questions that cannot be \nanswered by quantitative research methods, such as “how” and “why” a given \nintervention produces its effects. Qualitative evidence can help explain, \ninterpret and apply the quantitative results of a systematic review. A synthesis of the findings from qualitative research can be done as part of the \nscoping of the guideline and can help to define and refine the key questions. \nQualitative data may also inform the interpretation of studies on both benefits and harm, address questions on the contextual barriers and faci",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains how qualitative research can answer how and why questions, help interpret quantitative results, inform scoping, and illuminate barriers, facilitators, values, preferences and unintended social consequences. It points readers to the GRC intranet site and Cochrane resources for further guidance.",
        "state": "draft",
