      "target": "../sections/sec-149-88-systematic-review-quality-standards.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Regardless of the supplier selected, systematic reviews used to inform WHO \nrecommendations must be developed according to the standards outlined by \nthe Cochrane Collaboration in the Cochrane handbook (22). This handbook \nhas a chapter dealing with reviews in public health and health promotion. \nThe evidence-informed standards developed by the Institute of Medicine \nof the United States also provide a useful list of elements for high-quality \nreviews (30).",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
