    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-163",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Factors that determine the direction and strength of recommendations",
      "pageStart": 135,
      "pageEnd": 135,
      "target": "../sections/sec-163-101-factors-that-determine-the-direction-and-str.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "of recommendations\nFour main factors determine the direction and strength of a recommendation in public health (1–5):\n■■\nthe confidence in the estimates of effect of the evaluated evidence (i.e. \nthe quality of the evidence) (see Chapter 9);\n■■\nvalues and preferences related to the outcomes of an intervention or \nexposure;\n■■\nthe balance of benefits and harms; and\n■■\nresource implications.\nIn addition to these four main factors, several other considerations are \nimportant when formulating public health, health system and health policy \nrecommendations. These factors overlap with the main four",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Names the four main factors that determine the direction and strength of a recommendation: quality of the evidence, values and preferences, the balance of benefits and harms, and resource implications. It begins a list of four further considerations that GDGs may discuss separately, starting with the priority of the problem.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
