      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Developing recommendations",
      "pageStart": 135,
      "pageEnd": 136,
      "target": "../sections/sec-164-10-developing-recommendations.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "123\nWHO handbook for guideline development\n124\n124\n■■\nequity and human rights;\n■■\nacceptability; and\n■■\nfeasibility.\nTable 10.1 lists the detailed GRADE criteria that determine the direction and strength of a recommendation and describes how they influence the recommendation. These criteria are also included in the GRADE \nguideline development tool (6). To formulate a recommendation, the GDG \nconsiders each factor in turn and judges its importance and effect on the \nrecommendation.\nTable 10.1.\t Factors that determine the direction and strength of a \nrecommendation\nFactor\nHow the factor influen",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Continues the list of additional considerations (equity and human rights, acceptability and feasibility) and says Table 10.1 sets out the GRADE criteria the GDG considers in turn to judge each factor's effect. The extraction mostly contains page numbers, running headers and the table's column headings.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
