      "target": "../sections/sec-165-1021-quality-of-the-evidence.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The quality of the evidence across outcomes critical to decision-making will inform the \nstrength of the recommendation. The higher the quality of the evidence, the greater the \nlikelihood of a strong recommendation.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "States, as the first row of Table 10.1, that the quality of the evidence across critical outcomes informs recommendation strength, with higher quality making a strong recommendation more likely.",
