      "target": "../sections/sec-223-1117-references.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "1.\t\nKhangura S, Konnyu K, Cushman R, Grimshaw J, Moher D. Evidence summaries: the evolution of a rapid review approach. Syst Rev. 2012;1(1):10.\n2.\t\nWatt A, Cameron A, Sturm L, Lathlean T, Babidge W, Blamey S, et al. Rapid reviews versus \nfull systematic reviews: an inventory of current methods and practice in health technology assessment. Int J Technol Assess Health Care. 2008;24(2):133–9. doi: http://dx.doi.\norg/10.1017/S0266462308080185 PMID: 18400114\n3.\t\nGanann R, Ciliska D, Thomas H. Expediting systematic reviews: methods and implications \nof rapid reviews. Implement Sci. 2010;5(1):56. doi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A reference list of publications and WHO documents cited in the chapter on rapid advice guidelines, followed by the opening lines of the next chapter on producing and publishing the guideline, which begin a list of what needs coordinating.",
