    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-233",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Printing",
      "pageStart": 172,
      "pageEnd": 173,
      "target": "../sections/sec-233-1236-printing.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "12.3.5 Layout\nOnce you have an edited and carefully checked manuscript that has received \nfull executive clearance from the relevant assistant director-general, you will \nneed to send it for layout. Again, WHO Press can advise on external typesetters and the specifications that you should include when contracting for this \nwork. The WHO graphics team also provides an internal layout service. As \nmany design decisions have major implications for the cost of production, \nprinting, dissemination and subsequent translations, it is worth using existing publication templates if your department has e",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the layout and printing steps after executive clearance: using external typesetters or the graphics team and existing templates, then obtaining a cover, ISBN and barcode. Explains that the publishing office arranges printing quotes and print runs and that the proofreader should check the printer's proofs.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-234",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Disseminating guidelines",
      "pageStart": 173,
      "pageEnd": 173,
      "target": "../sections/sec-234-124-disseminating-guidelines.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Dissemination involves making guidelines accessible, advertising their \navailability and distributing them widely. Guideline developers should consult with WHO Press on priced and mandatory free distribution. Priced distribution is done by WHO Press through sales agents in all regions and by \nthe WHO bookshop. The extent of mandatory free distribution depends on \nthe type of publication but can include depository libraries, schools of public \nhealth, schools of medicine, WHO country offices and missions in Geneva. \nPlease consult with WHO Press on the number of print copies required for \nmanda",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that dissemination means making guidelines accessible, advertising them and distributing them, with priced distribution through sales agents and the bookshop and mandatory free distribution to bodies such as libraries and country offices, to be planned with the publishing office.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-235",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Online publication",
      "pageStart": 173,
      "pageEnd": 174,
      "target": "../sections/sec-235-1241-online-publication.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Your guideline can appear on the Internet in a variety of formats. At a minimum, you should contract your designer or typesetter to produce a web-\nready portable document format (PDF) – a smaller file size than the PDFs \nproduced for print – that is easier to download and navigate. Depending on \nthe length of the guideline and its intended audience, you may also wish to \nconsider providing full-text hypertext mark-up language (HTML) and additional materials, both electronic and printed. The WHO web team is a good \nsource of advice.\nWHO handbook for guideline development\n162\n162",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Advises producing at least a web-ready PDF of the guideline, possibly with HTML and extra materials, and consulting the WHO web team.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-236",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Archiving",
      "pageStart": 174,
      "pageEnd": 174,
      "target": "../sections/sec-236-1242-archiving.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "At the time of publication, the department should ensure that archiving \nrequirements are met. In headquarters, departments should send the final \nelectronic file of their guideline to the WHO Library for inclusion in the Institutional Repository for Information Sharing (IRIS) (4). In regional offices, \ndepartments should send the final electronic file of their information products to their regional office library. If printed copies are produced, one should \nalso be sent for inclusion in the print collection of the respective library.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes archiving requirements: departments send the final electronic file to the WHO Library repository, or regional office library, with a printed copy for the print collection if produced.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-237",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Translations",
      "pageStart": 174,
      "pageEnd": 174,
      "target": "../sections/sec-237-1243-translations.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Because WHO guidelines target a global audience, it is often necessary to \nprovide the guideline in one or several languages, particularly the six official languages; Arabic, Chinese, English, French, Russian and Spanish. To \nensure accurate translation of technical content, experts should be involved \nin checking the translations. Translations must be planned in advance \nand their timing discussed with the translation suppliers or regional office \ninvolved. Do not forget to budget for translation costs. To reduce such costs, \ntranslations may be limited to the executive summaries. Special car",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that translations, particularly into the six official languages, should be planned and budgeted, with experts checking technical content. Notes that translating only executive summaries can cut costs and that the meaning and strength of recommendations must not change.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-238",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Journals",
      "pageStart": 174,
      "pageEnd": 174,
      "target": "../sections/sec-238-1244-journals.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The systematic reviews commissioned for the guideline may be submitted for \npublication in the Bulletin of the World Health Organization or other journals. Cochrane reviews are published in the Cochrane Library. To increase \nawareness of the guideline, the guideline development process and/or recommendations may also be published in peer-reviewed journals, in compliance \nwith WHO’s open access and copyright policies. All external publications \nwith WHO authors require internal clearance.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that the commissioned systematic reviews and the guideline's process or recommendations may be published in journals, within open access and copyright policy, and that external publications with WHO authors require internal clearance.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-239",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Other forms of dissemination",
      "pageStart": 174,
      "pageEnd": 175,
      "target": "../sections/sec-239-1245-other-forms-of-dissemination.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "You should carefully plan a dissemination strategy early in the development \nprocess. A variety of approaches should be considered. These can include an offi\nChapter 12 \nProducing and publishing the guideline\n163\n163\ncial launch, a press release and/or conference, an announcement on the WHO \nwebsite, distribution through regional offices or at meetings, and endorsement \nby stakeholders and interest groups. Mobile phone applications for guideline \ndissemination and decision support can also be commissioned. Because the \nguideline document itself may be quite lengthy, more succinct derivative pr",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Advises planning a dissemination strategy early, using launches, press releases, web announcements, regional distribution, stakeholder endorsement and mobile applications, and preparing shorter derivative products such as charts and manuals.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
