      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Updating guideline",
      "pageStart": 175,
      "pageEnd": 175,
      "target": "../sections/sec-240-125-updating-guideline.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "empty"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-241",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Review-by date",
      "pageStart": 175,
      "pageEnd": 175,
      "target": "../sections/sec-241-1251-review-by-date.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "WHO guidelines should be issued with a “review-by” date to indicate how long the \nrecommendations are expected to remain valid. There is no absolute rule about \nthe length of validity (5, 6). In deciding on the date by which a guideline should be \nreviewed, take account of the rate of change of research on the topic, questions for \nwhich no evidence has been found, and the potential need for new advice.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Explains that guidelines should carry a review-by date showing how long recommendations are expected to stay valid, set by considering the pace of research, questions without evidence and the potential need for new advice.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-10-06"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/9789241548960-eng/blocks/prose-sec-242",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Updating recommendations",
      "pageStart": 175,
      "pageEnd": 175,
      "target": "../sections/sec-242-1252-updating-recommendations.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "All WHO recommendations that are not based on the processes and standards outlined in this handbook (particularly those published before the GRC \nwas established in 2007 and those not considering equity, human rights and \ngender) should be updated to meet current WHO guideline standards. Updating guidelines is challenging if evidence has to be retrieved to support a large \nnumber of existing recommendations. In this situation it is important to give \npriority to controversial areas, or those in which new evidence has emerged. If \nrecommendations will be updated incrementally, the planned appro",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
